{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Fill his house with silver and gold.</b> We learn that he was greedy and coveted others' money — he said: It is fitting for him to give me all his silver and gold, since he must hire many soldiers, perhaps he wins, perhaps he does not win, and I will certainly win (there)." "<b>I am not able to go beyond.</b> Against his will he revealed that he is under the authority of others, and he prophesied here that he cannot annul the blessings with which the patriarchs were blessed from the mouth of the Shechinah (there)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:11.977623521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}